/-!
# MiniRust in Lean, and its correspondence with Anneal's MIR semantics

* `MiniRustSpec.Generated` (generated by `crates/anneal-minirust-gen` from the
  vendored, pinned MiniRust sources; never edited by hand): one Lean item per
  upstream Rust item, as a deep embedding of its syntax plus shallow Lean
  types for the spec's data types.
* `MiniRustSpec.Interp`: an executable interpretation of a small subset of the
  spec, transcribed by hand with quotations; `MiniRustSpec.Anchors` pins every
  transcribed upstream item to the generated model.
* `MiniRustSpec.Correspondence.*`: the correspondence between Anneal's MIR
  semantics (`Trusted.Rustc.V2026_06_01`) and that interpretation, with
  non-vacuity witnesses (`Correspondence.Witness`); `Correspondence.Pointers`
  (with its submodules `Correspondence.PointersCore`, `Correspondence.PointersLattice`,
  `Correspondence.PointersMachineCodec`, `Correspondence.PointersMachineExpr`,
  `Correspondence.PointersMachineStep`, and `Correspondence.PointersMachine`)
  and `Correspondence.PointerStep` relate the two semantics on the raw pointer
  and reference statements the fragment admits (`&raw`, `&`, `&mut`,
  reborrowing `&*_p` / `&mut *_p` / `&raw *_p`, pointer copies, and reads and
  writes through pointers and references, including `move` rvalues and
  pointer-to-pointer dereference copies) and prove structural Tree Borrows
  (`TreeBorrowsMemory.wf` / `wfLive` and panic-freedom) invariants, while
  `Correspondence.PointerWitness`, `Correspondence.RefWitness`, and
  `Correspondence.TbWitness` compare Anneal, `Machine<BasicMemory>`, and
  `Machine<TreeBorrowsMemory>` on concrete raw pointer, reference, reborrowing,
  safe-pointer validity, `CastKind.transmute`, `Box<T>`, `UnsafeCell<T>`,
  `IntPtrCast`, and Tree Borrows programs; `Correspondence.Provenance` and
  `Correspondence.ProvenanceWitness` cover the integer-pointer provenance casts;
  the multi-function relation (`Terminator::Call`, call stacks, and the
  `Assume` intrinsic) is proven in `Correspondence.Simulation` and
  `Correspondence.Run`, with witnesses for intrinsic calls that resolve to MIR
  fallback bodies (`Correspondence.IntrinsicFallback`), wide-slice and unsized
  DST pointer-metadata correspondence (`Correspondence.WideSliceDst`), and
  boundary witnesses for the intrinsic constructs outside the fragment
  (`Correspondence.IntrinsicBoundary`).
* `MiniRustSpec.UnwindSetDiscrAndFnPtrMR`: correspondence, `MachTB.wfLive`
  preservation, `Classical.choice`-free codecs, and boundary/divergence
  characterizations across `Mach` and `MachTB` for
  `Statement.SetDiscriminant`, `Terminator.{StartUnwind, StopUnwind,
  ResumeUnwind}`, `unwindResume`, `unwindTerminate`, `coverage`,
  `backwardIncompatibleDropHint`, `fnPtrToPtr`, `subtype`, non-`Unsize`
  `pointerCoercion` (`ReifyFnPointer`, `ClosureFnPointer`, `UnsafeFnPointer`,
  `MutToConstPointer`, `ArrayToPointer`), `unwrapUnsafeBinder`, and
  `AggregateKind.closure`.
* `MiniRustSpec.FloatArithMR`: two-sided fail-closed translation boundary for
  float unary negation and binary arithmetic/comparison ops (including
  no-float-local float-constant comparison rejection, arbitrary projected
  float places `*p` / `_s.0` / `_a[i]`, and the exact two-sided
  `translateRvalue` truth `fa_translateRvalue_binaryOp_two_sided`), IEEE-754
  bit-carrier bridges (`UnOp.neg` ↔ `u32`/`u64` sign-bit XOR lockstep across
  `Mach` and `MachTB` with `MachTB.wfLive`, `Bool` comparison carriers, and
  `EvalFloatBinOpRel` / `nanChoices` `.deterministic` & `.nondeterministic`
  carriers, with universal `f64` 8-byte, zero-extended `f32`, and native
  4-byte `f32` `Mach` + `MachTB.wfLive` carrier execution), mode-parametric
  `Ptr2IntTransmutePolicy` (`ucg#630` vs.
  `reference#1752`) scalar and composite `(*const u8, usize)` / `struct Mixed`
  correspondence across `BasicMemory` and `TreeBorrowsMemory`, shared UB /
  no-forgery (`usize → &u8`, `MaybeUninit` uninit → `u64`, size mismatch), and
  shared concrete witnesses `W1–W6` (68 public theorems, all pinned by
  `axiomAudit_choiceFree` and `axiomAudit_machine`).
* `MiniRustSpec.ClosureFnPtrMR`: dual-authority correspondence for
  non-capturing closure function pointers. Universal laws relate `Trusted`'s
  callee-directed closure dispatch (`calleeOwnClosureShape?`, no closure flag
  on `FnPtrEntry`, synthesized zero-sized environment prepended to `_1`) to
  MiniRust functions of the closure's user-visible arity across `Mach` and
  `MachTB` (`ClosureFnPtrEntryRel`, `ClosureFnSigRel`,
  `ClosureFnPointer(Safe|Unsafe)` reification, `UnsafeFnPointer` widening,
  `FnPtrToPtr` pointer identity, indirect `call` / `tailCall` for `Fn` /
  `FnMut` / `FnOnce` receivers, the `const_eval_select` runtime target,
  translation-derived fixed-width integer/`bool` ABI correspondence, and the
  fail-closed capturing, forged `(N + 1)`-argument, ABI, `Safety`,
  generic-closure, and direct-call laws), with non-vacuity instantiations and
  kernel-checked three-way witnesses on verbatim `rustc-capture` bodies —
  including the difftest reproducer that Miri evaluates to `9147` and
  characterization of the pre-existing thin-pointer / `usize`-vs-`u64`
  false-positive UB divergence (pinned by `#assert_closure_fn_ptr_mr_audit` and
  `[CLOSURE-FNPTR-AUDIT]`).
* `MiniRustSpec.Audit`: fails the build unless the main theorems use only the
  standard axioms.

See `minirust/README.md`.
-/
